.TH FILE-ORGANIZER 1 "December 2025" "Version 1.0" "File Organizer"
.SH NAME
file-organizer \- organize files in directories by type/category
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B file-organizer
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B file-organizer
is a utility that automatically organizes files in a directory by their types and categories.
It creates category folders and moves files appropriately, helping to maintain a clean file structure.
.PP
The tool is safe to use as it validates input paths and prevents organization of root directories.
It handles filename conflicts automatically and provides detailed feedback during the organization process.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Run in quiet mode (suppress most output).
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Automatically answer yes to all prompts.
.SH FILE CATEGORIES
The organizer categorizes files into the following types:
.TP
.B Images
\.jpg, \.jpeg, \.png, \.gif, \.bmp, \.tiff, \.svg, \.webp, \.ico, \.raw
.TP
.B Documents
\.pdf, \.doc, \.docx, \.txt, \.rtf, \.odt, \.pages, \.tex
.TP
.B Spreadsheets
\.xls, \.xlsx, \.csv, \.ods, \.numbers
.TP
.B Presentations
\.ppt, \.pptx, \.odp, \.key
.TP
.B Videos
\.mp4, \.avi, \.mkv, \.mov, \.wmv, \.flv, \.webm, \.m4v, \.3gp
.TP
.B Audio
\.mp3, \.wav, \.flac, \.aac, \.ogg, \.wma, \.m4a, \.opus
.TP
.B Archives
\.zip, \.rar, \.7z, \.tar, \.gz, \.bz2, \.xz, \.iso
.TP
.B Code
\.py, \.js, \.html, \.css, \.java, \.cpp, \.c, \.php, \.rb, \.go, \.rs
.TP
.B Executables
\.exe, \.msi, \.deb, \.rpm, \.dmg, \.app, \.run, \.sh
.TP
.B CAD Files
\.dwg, \.dxf, \.step, \.stp, \.iges, \.igs, \.obj, \.stl
.TP
.B Data Files
\.json, \.xml, \.yaml, \.yml, \.sql, \.db, \.sqlite, \.xlsx
.TP
.B eBooks
\.epub, \.mobi, \.azw, \.azw3, \.lit, \.fb2
.TP
.B Others
Any file types not listed above
.SH USAGE
When run without options, \fBfile-organizer\fR will:
.IP 1. 3
Ask for a directory path to organize
.IP 2. 3
Validate that the path is not a root directory
.IP 3. 3
Show the current files in the directory
.IP 4. 3
Create category folders
.IP 5. 3
Move files to appropriate categories
.IP 6. 3
Provide a summary of the organization
.PP
The tool will create folders like \fIImages/\fR, \fIDocuments/\fR, \fIVideos/\fR, etc., and move files into the appropriate categories.
.SH EXAMPLES
Organize files in the Downloads directory:
.IP
.B file-organizer
.PP
The tool will prompt for a path. Enter a directory such as:
.IP
.B /home/username/Downloads
.PP
Files will be organized into category folders like:
.IP
.nf
Downloads/
├── Images/
│   └── photo.jpg
├── Documents/
│   └── report.pdf
├── Audio/
│   └── song.mp3
└── Videos/
    └── video.mp4
.fi
.SH SAFETY FEATURES
.IP \(bu
Root directory protection - prevents organization of system directories
.IP \(bu
Path validation - ensures paths exist and are directories
.IP \(bu
Conflict resolution - handles duplicate filenames automatically
.IP \(bu
Error handling - graceful handling of errors and user cancellation
.IP \(bu
Preview - shows current files before organization
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
User home directory (used for default paths)
.TP
.B PATH
Installation directories are added to PATH if needed
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $INSTALL_BIN/file-organizer
The main executable script
.TP
.B $INSTALL_MAN/file-organizer.1
This manual page
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful organization
.TP
.B 1
General error (invalid path, permission denied, etc.)
.TP
.B 2
User cancellation
